A||||3||88Style||Steering wheel play||||1||
Z||000000||88Style||11-02-2001||03:06 PM||||Looking for some expert advice, my 88 Formula has a lot of steering wheel play. It has a great ratio but I am getting an inch or so each way at the steering wheel before the car turns. Anyone have any ideas on this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||11-02-2001||04:16 PM||||I had that problem in my Formula. Root cause was a bad adjustment in the R&P preload nut. It is the big nut cap that you see near the top of the R&P at the shaft area. Is not too easy to adjust. Too much one way and steering gets pretty hard. What I end up doing was disconecting the shaft from the column and slowly adjusted it whlie moving the shaft (with visegrip) and measuring play.<BR>Have in mind that also the actual rack (inside) may be worn. If car has many miles probably would be better to just replace it.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000002||88Style||11-02-2001||04:22 PM||||Thank you!!! I had done a search before and seen mention of the preload. The rack is pretty new but the car sat idle for a long time. The previous rack actually had the nut fall off and loose some of the guts of the rack. I will get up there and adjust it. Tighten it and the steering gets tighter or the other way around?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-02-2001||05:08 PM||||I had to do the same thing with my 88 coupe. <BR>It helped a little, but I think the rack is just too worn. <BR>If I remember correctly, the adjustment is actually like a big nut/locknut affair. Loosen the "outer" locknut just a bit. Then tighten the center nut. Not sure about the specs, though. Might be useful to take the nut out and grease the slider bushing where it presses against the rack. Don't know if I'm using the right terms or not, but you'll see what I mean.<BR>This is waaaay easier to do if you remove the plastic well from the front compartment.<BR>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
